  "comment": "MiniMax H3 Turbo (BETA), API format. Same graph contract as minimax-h3.api.json plus larryvrh's turbo distill LoRA at minimax_h3_turbo_v4_step600_ema \u2014 upstream's current recommendation \u2014 applied by UPSTREAM'S OWN LOADER, MiniMaxH3TurboLoRA (node 40). That loader is mandatory: ComfyUI's plain LoraLoaderModelOnly cannot apply this LoRA to our PRUNED int8-convrot base because the 51 AdaLN pairs have no home, which is why this graph previously shipped drbaph's ckpt500 conversion with those adapters STRIPPED and its own metadata warning that 4-step behaviour 'may be degraded or broken'. Upstream's loader detects the pruned base and re-injects the time conditioning from the h3_silu_temb_grid.safetensors shipped with the node, so all 259 pairs apply intact. strength 1.0, scheduler simple, 6 steps (upstream: 4 is the minimum, 4-8 the useful range; at 4 steps with heavy motion v4-600 can smear). low_vram OFF applies the LoRA at run time \u2014 turn it ON only if the card OOMs, since merging rounds the delta away on a quantized base, which is exactly this one. We do NOT use upstream's MiniMaxH3TurboSampler: measured on a rented 5090 it bypasses Spectrum's sampler hooks, so every step becomes a real eval \u2014 61s of sampling against 30s through KSamplerSelect/euler with the manual dual sigma shift restored. On a ComfyUI recent enough to schedule audio natively (ours, e377e263) their sampler is documented to behave as a stock sampler anyway, and MiniMaxH3SigmaShift video=12 audio=6 supplies the dual schedule as it always did \u2014 verified by audio measurement, mean -32.7 dB / max -7.1 dB, louder and un-clipped against the old LoRA's -45.2/-20.0. MODEL chain: UNETLoader(6) -> MiniMaxH3TurboLoRA(40) -> PathchSageAttentionKJ(31) -> MiniMaxH3SigmaShift(43) -> Spectrum(30) -> scheduler+guider. Benchmarked at ~80s for a 5s 960x544 clip against 98s for the minimax-h3 quality tier. Keep minimax-h3 as the quality tier.",
